#!/bin/sh /etc/rc.common
# procd service for MudiModem's daemon + collector: RF + battery history in /tmp/mudimodem, the
# eMMC backup, the live pushes, and the AT console's queue. Respawned on crash.
#
# mudimodemd (GL's own lua-eco, /usr/bin/eco, in the 4.10 image) always runs: it is the
# collector AND the AT console's queue (`ubus call mudimodem …`, which the RPC plugin forwards
# to). Its collector needs no Python, so live data works straight after a firmware upgrade,
# before the deps healer has reinstalled python3. The Python collector stays as the escape
# hatch: put the word `python` in /etc/mudimodem/collector and it samples instead, while
# mudimodemd runs with its collector off (both write the same files and pushes:
# test/collectd-emu.test.py runs them side by side on an emulated GL bus).

START=95
STOP=10
USE_PROCD=1
DAEMON=/usr/sbin/mudimodemd
PROG=/usr/sbin/mudimodem-collectd
DEPS=/usr/lib/mudimodem/mudimodem-deps
ENGINE_FILE=/etc/mudimodem/collector

engine() {
	if [ "$(cat "$ENGINE_FILE" 2>/dev/null)" != python ] && [ -x /usr/bin/eco ] && [ -f "$DAEMON" ]; then
		echo eco
	else
		echo python
	fi
}

start_service() {
	local e
	e=$(engine)
	if [ -x /usr/bin/eco ] && [ -f "$DAEMON" ]; then
		procd_open_instance mudimodemd
		procd_set_param command /usr/bin/eco "$DAEMON"
		[ "$e" = eco ] || procd_set_param env MUDIMODEMD_COLLECTOR=0
		procd_set_param respawn
		procd_set_param stderr 1
		procd_close_instance
	fi
	[ "$e" = python ] || return 0
	# No python3 (a firmware upgrade wipes opkg packages): let the healer
	# install it and start us, instead of respawning into "not found".
	if ! "$DEPS" check; then
		/usr/lib/mudimodem/mudimodem-detach "$DEPS" heal &
		return 0
	fi
	procd_open_instance collector
	procd_set_param command /usr/bin/python3 "$PROG"
	procd_set_param respawn
	procd_set_param stderr 1
	procd_close_instance
}
